From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] malloc/memory: include <unistd.h> for POSIX fns

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/v6d-io/v6d/pull/TODO]

Real riscv64 CI (this PR's own run, "Configure and build vineyardd" step)
fails both files identically, once the earlier gRPC OOM fix (-j2 cap) lets
the build get far enough to actually compile them:

    src/server/memory/malloc.cc:221:17: error: 'lseek' was not declared
    src/server/memory/malloc.cc:223:9: error: 'ftruncate' was not declared
    src/server/memory/malloc.cc:295:5: error: 'close' was not declared
    src/server/memory/memory.cc:58:19: error: 'sysconf' was not declared
    src/server/memory/memory.cc:58:27: error: '_SC_PAGESIZE' was not declared

Both files use these POSIX functions/macros without including <unistd.h>
that declares them; neither file's other includes (<dlfcn.h>, <fcntl.h>,
<sys/mman.h>, gflags, logging.h) pull it in transitively on this riscv64
toolchain's glibc/GCC combination, though they evidently do on whatever
glibc/GCC v6d's own CI builds against (this fleet is the only riscv64 CI
this package has ever run on). Add the missing include to both.

---
 src/server/memory/malloc.cc | 1 +
 src/server/memory/memory.cc | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/server/memory/malloc.cc b/src/server/memory/malloc.cc
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/server/memory/malloc.cc
+++ b/src/server/memory/malloc.cc
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include <dlfcn.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <sys/mman.h>
+#include <unistd.h>

 #include <stddef.h>
 #include <string>
diff --git a/src/server/memory/memory.cc b/src/server/memory/memory.cc
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/server/memory/memory.cc
+++ b/src/server/memory/memory.cc
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 #include "server/memory/memory.h"

 #include <sys/mman.h>
+#include <unistd.h>

 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cstdint>
--
2.43.0
